235\" y=\"71\">6.5</text><text x=\"285\" y=\"71\">3.9</text><text x=\"335\" y=\"71\">4.8</text><text x=\"385\" y=\"71\">7.0</text><text x=\"35\" y=\"107\">6.6</text><text x=\"85\" y=\"107\">5.0</text><text x=\"135\" y=\"107\">5.1</text><text x=\"185\" y=\"107\">6.9</text><text x=\"235\" y=\"107\">5.3</text><text x=\"285\" y=\"107\">7.9</text><text x=\"335\" y=\"107\">6.4</text><text x=\"385\" y=\"107\">4.1</text><text x=\"35\" y=\"143\">7.2</text><text x=\"85\" y=\"143\">3.5</text><text x=\"135\" y=\"143\">6.0</text><text x=\"185\" y=\"143\">4.8</text><text x=\"235\" y=\"143\">6.7</text><text x=\"285\" y=\"143\">5.9</text><text x=\"335\" y=\"143\">4.7</text><text x=\"385\" y=\"143\">6.8</text></g></svg>", "number": "1", "question": ["A group of $32$ boys took part in a shot put competition. The table shows the distances (in meters) of their throws.", "(1) Draw a histogram, using $3$, $4$, $5$, $6$, $7$ and $8$ as the class boundaries. (Each class includes its lower boundary but not its upper boundary.)", "(2) Boys who threw less than $5.0$ m had to attend a training program. How many boys had to attend?", "(3) The best $10\\%$ of the boys will receive a prize. What should the minimum distance for a prize be?"], "section": "", "solution": ["(1) Sort the $32$ distances into the classes $[3,4)$, $[4,5)$, $[5,6)$, $[6,7)$, $[7,8)$.", "$[3,4)$: $3.2, 3.9, 3.5$, so the frequency is $3$.", "$[4,5)$: $4.2, 4.8, 4.1, 4.8, 4.7$, so the frequency is $5$.", "$[5,6)$: $5.3, 5.5, 5.9, 5.8, 5.0, 5.1, 5.3, 5.9$, so the frequency is $8$.", "$[6,7)$: $6.2, 6.8, 6.1, 6.4, 6.5, 6.6, 6.9, 6.4, 6.0, 6.7, 6.8$, so the frequency is $11$.", "$[7,8)$: $7.7, 7.6, 7.0, 7.9, 7.2$, so the frequency is $5$.", "Check the total: $3+5+8+11+5 = 32$.", "Draw adjacent bars of heights $3, 5, 8, 11, 5$ over the class intervals, with distance (m) on the horizontal axis and frequency on the vertical axis.", "(2) Throws less than $5.0$ m are in the classes $[3,4)$ and $[4,5)$.", "Number of boys: $3 + 5 = 8$.", "(3) $10\\%$ of $32$ is $0.1 \\times 32 = 3.2$, so the best $3$ boys receive a prize.", "The longest throws in order are $7.9, 7.7, 7.6, 7.2, \\dots$", "The third-best throw is $7.6$ m, so the minimum distance for a prize is $7.6$ m."], "topic": "Data and Uncertainty / Probability and Statistics", "type": "Worked example", "updatedAt": 1794901821400, "volume": "", "id": "33kq95didnvfanszvcm0"}, {"answer": ["The mean waiting time is $21.2$ minutes."], "answer_figures": [], "book": "NDM", "category": "Procedure", "chapter": 12, "createdAt": 1794907102734, "figure_svg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 420 280\" width=\"420\" height=\"280\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"420\" height=\"280\" fill=\"white\"/><g data-grid=\"1\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M57.00 100V200M74.00 100V200M91.00 100V200M108.00 100V200M142.00 100V200M159.00 100V200M176.00 100V200M193.00 100V200M227.00 100V200M244.00 100V200M261.00 100V200M278.00 100V200M312.00 100V200M329.00 100V200M346.00 100V200M363.00 100V200\" stroke=\"#bcd7e6\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><path d=\"M40.00 100V200M125.00 100V200M210.00 100V200M295.00 100V200M380.00 100V200M40 200.00H380M40 180.00H380M40 160.00H380M40 140.00H380M40 120.00H380M40 100.00H380\" stroke=\"#7fb0cb\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/></g><text x=\"210\" y=\"45\" font-family=\"Times New Roman, serif\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Waiting times of patients at a clinic</text><line x1=\"25\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"200\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"2\"><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"210\"/><line x1=\"125\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"125\" y2=\"210\"/><line x1=\"210\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"210\" y2=\"210\"/><line x1=\"295\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"295\" y2=\"210\"/><line x1=\"380\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"210\"/></g><g stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><line x1=\"57\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"57\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"74\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"74\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"91\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"91\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"108\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"108\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"142\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"142\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"159\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"159\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"176\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"176\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"193\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"193\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"227\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"227\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"244\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"244\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"261\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"261\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"278\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"278\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"312\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"312\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"329\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"329\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"346\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"346\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"363\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"363\" y2=\"205\"/></g><g font-family=\"Times New Roman, serif\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"40\" y=\"232\">10</text><text x=\"125\" y=\"232\">15</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"232\">20</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"232\">25</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"232\">30</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"265\">Waiting time (minutes)</text></g><g fill=\"black\"><circle cx=\"57\" cy=\"180\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"108\" cy=\"180\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"125\" cy=\"180\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"125\" cy=\"160\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"159\" cy=\"180\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"193\" cy=\"180\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"244\" cy=\"180\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"244\" cy=\"160\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"295\" cy=\"180\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"295\" cy=\"160\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"295\" cy=\"140\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"295\" cy=\"120\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"329\" cy=\"180\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"329\" cy=\"160\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"363\" cy=\"180\" r=\"6\"/></g></svg>", "number": "4", "question": ["The dot diagram shows the waiting times, in minutes, of some patients at a clinic. Find the mean waiting time of the patients."], "section": "12.1", "solution": ["Read the data from the dot diagram: $11$, $14$, $15$, $15$, $17$, $19$, $22$, $22$, $25$, $25$, $25$, $25$, $27$, $27$, $29$.", "Number of patients $= 1+1+2+1+1+2+4+2+1 = 15$", "Sum of waiting times $= 11 + 14 + 2(15) + 17 + 19 + 2(22) + 4(25) + 2(27) + 29$", "$= 11 + 14 + 30 + 17 + 19 + 44 + 100 + 54 + 29 = 318$", "Mean $= \\frac{318}{15} = 21.2$ minutes"], "topic": "", "type": "Worked example", "variants": [{"answer": ["The mean waiting time is $20$ minutes."], "answer_figures": [], "figure_svg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 420 280\" width=\"420\" height=\"280\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"420\" height=\"280\" fill=\"white\"/><g data-grid=\"1\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M57.00 100V200M74.00 100V200M91.00 100V200M108.00 100V200M142.00 100V200M159.00 100V200M176.00 100V200M193.00 100V200M227.00 100V200M244.00 100V200M261.00 100V200M278.00 100V200M312.00 100V200M329.00 100V200M346.00 100V200M363.00 100V200\" stroke=\"#bcd7e6\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><path d=\"M40.00 100V200M125.00 100V200M210.00 100V200M295.00 100V200M380.00 100V200M40 200.00H380M40 180.00H380M40 160.00H380M40 140.00H380M40 120.00H380M40 100.00H380\" stroke=\"#7fb0cb\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/></g><text x=\"210\" y=\"45\" font-family=\"Times New Roman, serif\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"bold\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Waiting times of patients at a clinic</text><line x1=\"25\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"395\" y2=\"200\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><g stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"2\"><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"40\" y2=\"210\"/><line x1=\"125\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"125\" y2=\"210\"/><line x1=\"210\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"210\" y2=\"210\"/><line x1=\"295\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"295\" y2=\"210\"/><line x1=\"380\" y1=\"190\" x2=\"380\" y2=\"210\"/></g><g stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><line x1=\"57\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"57\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"74\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"74\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"91\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"91\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"108\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"108\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"142\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"142\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"159\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"159\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"176\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"176\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"193\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"193\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"227\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"227\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"244\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"244\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"261\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"261\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"278\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"278\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"312\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"312\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"329\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"329\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"346\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"346\" y2=\"205\"/><line x1=\"363\" y1=\"195\" x2=\"363\" y2=\"205\"/></g><g font-family=\"Times New Roman, serif\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"40\" y=\"232\">10</text><text x=\"125\" y=\"232\">15</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"232\">20</text><text x=\"295\" y=\"232\">25</text><text x=\"380\" y=\"232\">30</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"265\">Waiting time (minutes)</text></g><g fill=\"black\"><circle cx=\"74\" cy=\"180\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"91\" cy=\"180\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"125\" cy=\"180\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"142\" cy=\"180\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"142\" cy=\"160\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"176\" cy=\"180\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"210\" cy=\"180\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"210\" cy=\"160\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"244\" cy=\"180\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"244\" cy=\"160\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"244\" cy=\"140\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"278\" cy=\"180\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"278\" cy=\"160\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"312\" cy=\"180\" r=\"6\"/><circle cx=\"380\" cy=\"180\" r=\"6\"/></g></svg>", "question": ["The dot diagram shows the waiting times, in minutes, of some patients at a clinic. Find the mean waiting time of the patients."], "solution": ["Read the data from the dot diagram: $12$, $13$, $15$, $16$, $16$, $18$, $20$, $20$, $22$, $22$, $22$, $24$, $24$, $26$, $30$.", "Number of patients $= 1+1+1+2+1+2+3+2+1+1 = 15$", "Sum of waiting times $= 12 + 13 + 15 + 2(16) + 18 + 2(20) + 3(22) + 2(24) + 26 + 30$", "$= 12 + 13 + 15 + 32 + 18 + 40 + 66 + 48 + 26 + 30 = 300$", "Mean $= \\frac{300}{15} = 20$ minutes"]}], "volume": "2", "id": "4ucd68oz0433dznkud0l"}, {"answer": ["The mean mass is $203$ g."], "answer_figures": [], "book": "NDM", "category": "Procedure", "chapter": 12, "createdAt": 1794906844166, "figure_svg": "", "number": "1", "question": ["The masses, in grams, of $6$ mangoes are as follows:", "$205, \\ 208, \\ 211, \\ 197, \\ 192, \\ 205$", "Find the mean mass of the mangoes."], "section": "12.1", "solution": ["Mean $= \\frac{\\text{sum of masses}}{\\text{number of mangoes}}$", "Sum $= 205 + 208 + 211 + 197 + 192 + 205$", "Sum $= 1218$", "Mean $= \\frac{1218}{6}$", "Mean $= 203$ g"], "topic": "", "type": "Worked example", "volume": "2", "id": "5eccww2gxqztbokq2nmx"}, {"answer": ["$\\frac{73}{24}$ (that is, $3\\frac{1}{24}$)"], "answer_figures": [], "book": "NDM", "category": "Procedure", "chapter": 2, "createdAt": 1794897844396, "figs_checked": false, "figure_svg": "", "number": "14", "question": ["$\\frac{7}{8}-\\left(-2\\frac{3}{4}\\right)+\\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)$."], "section": "2.5", "solution": ["Convert the mixed number: $2\\frac{3}{4}=\\frac{11}{4}$.", "Rewrite subtracting a negative as adding, and adding a negative as subtracting: $\\frac{7}{8}+\\frac{11}{4}-\\frac{1}{3}$.", "The lowest common denominator of $8$, $4$ and $3$ is $24$.", "$\\frac{7}{8}=\\frac{21}{24}$, $\\frac{11}{4}=\\frac{66}{24}$, $\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{8}{24}$.", "$\\frac{21+66-8}{24}=\\frac{79}{24}$.", "So the result is $\\frac{79}{24}=3\\frac{7}{24}$."], "topic": "", "type": "Worked example", "updatedAt": 1794905639176, "volume": "1", "id": "6pa2ye80c0vwgafeyk3m"}, {"answer": ["$172.5$ cm"], "answer_figures": [], "book": "NDM", "category": "Procedure", "chapter": 12, "createdAt": 1794906892701, "figure_svg": "", "number": "2", "question": ["The mean height of $5$ basketball players is $178$ cm. The mean height of $11$ soccer players is $170$ cm. Find the mean height of all these players."], "section": "12.1", "solution": ["Total height of the basketball players $= 5 \\times 178 = 890$ cm", "Total height of the soccer players $= 11 \\times 170 = 1870$ cm", "Total height of all players $= 890 + 1870 = 2760$ cm", "Total number of players $= 5 + 11 = 16$", "Mean height of all players $= \\frac{2760}{16} = 172.5$ cm"], "topic": "", "type": "Worked example", "volume": "2", "id": "9tgnodnzqkk0nwf5psmv"}, {"answer": ["(1) Restaurant A: $p = 42\\%$; Restaurant B: $p = 8\\%$", "(2) Restaurant A: $x = 40$; Restaurant B: $x = 20$", "(3) Restaurant A: $x = \\frac{480}{13} \\approx 36.9$; Restaurant B: $x = \\frac{205}{9} \\approx 22.8$"], "answer_figures": [], "book": "FREE", "category": "Procedure", "chapter": "", "createdAt": 1794902616660, "figure_svg": "<svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 480 680' width='480' height='680'><rect x='0' y='0' width='480' height='680' fill='white'/><g data-grid=\"1\" fill=\"none\"><path d=\"M84.00 50V610M98.00 50V610M112.00 50V610M126.00 50V610M154.00 50V610M168.00 50V610M182.00 50V610M196.00 50V610M224.00 50V610M238.00 50V610M252.00 50V610M266.00 50V610M294.00 50V610M308.00 50V610M322.00 50V610M336.00 50V610M364.00 50V610M378.00 50V610M392.00 50V610M406.00 50V610M70 602.00H420M70 594.00H420M70 586.00H420M70 578.00H420M70 562.00H420M70 554.00H420M70 546.00H420M70 538.00H420M70 522.00H420M70 514.00H420M70 506.00H420M70 498.00H420M70 482.00H420M70 474.00H420M70 466.00H420M70 458.00H420M70 442.00H420M70 434.00H420M70 426.00H420M70 418.00H420M70 402.00H420M70 394.00H420M70 386.00H420M70 378.00H420M70 362.00H420M70 354.00H420M70 346.00H420M70 338.00H420M70 322.00H420M70 314.00H420M70 306.00H420M70 298.00H420M70 282.00H420M70 274.00H420M70 266.00H420M70 258.00H420M70 242.00H420M70 234.00H420M70 226.00H420M70 218.00H420M70 202.00H420M70 194.00H420M70 186.00H420M70 178.00H420M70 162.00H420M70 154.00H420M70 146.00H420M70 138.00H420M70 122.00H420M70 114.00H420M70 106.00H420M70 98.00H420M70 82.00H420M70 74.00H420M70 66.00H420M70 58.00H420\" stroke=\"#bcd7e6\" stroke-width=\"0.7\"/><path d=\"M70.00 50V610M140.00 50V610M210.00 50V610M280.00 50V610M350.00 50V610M420.00 50V610M70 610.00H420M70 570.00H420M70 530.00H420M70 490.00H420M70 450.00H420M70 410.00H420M70 370.00H420M70 330.00H420M70 290.00H420M70 250.00H420M70 210.00H420M70 170.00H420M70 130.00H420M70 90.00H420M70 50.00H420\" stroke=\"#7fb0cb\" stroke-width=\"1.2\"/></g><g font-family='Times New Roman, serif' font-size='18' fill='black'><text x='245' y='30' text-anchor='middle'>Waiting times of customers at Restaurant A</text><g stroke='black' stroke-width='2' fill='#dddddd'><rect x='140' y='210' width='70' height='40'/><rect x='210' y='162' width='70' height='88'/><rect x='280' y='146' width='70' height='104'/><rect x='350' y='82' width='70' height='168'/></g><g stroke='black' stroke-width='2' fill='none'><path d='M70 250H440M70 250V42'/><path d='M63 250H70M63 210H70M63 170H70M63 130H70M63 90H70M63 50H70'/><path d='M70 250V257M140 250V257M210 250V257M280 250V257M350 250V257M420 250V257'/></g><g text-anchor='middle'><text x='70' y='276'>0</text><text x='140' y='276'>10</text><text x='210' y='276'>20</text><text x='280' y='276'>30</text><text x='350' y='276'>40</text><text x='420' y='276'>50</text></g><g text-anchor='end'><text x='58' y='216'>5</text><text x='58' y='176'>10</text><text x='58' y='136'>15</text><text x='58' y='96'>20</text><text x='58' y='56'>25</text></g><text x='245' y='302' text-anchor='middle'>Waiting time (min)</text><text x='24' y='150' text-anchor='middle' transform='rotate(-90 24 150)'>Frequency</text><text x='245' y='388' text-anchor='middle'>Waiting times of customers at Restaurant B</text><g stroke='black' stroke-width='2' fill='#dddddd'><rect x='140' y='450' width='70' height='160'/><rect x='210' y='466' width='70' height='144'/><rect x='280' y='546' width='70' height='64'/><rect x='350' y='578' width='70' height='32'/></g><g stroke='black' stroke-width='2' fill='none'><path d='M70 610H440M70 610V402'/><path d='M63 610H70M63 570H70M63 530H70M63 490H70M63 450H70M63 410H70'/><path d='M70 610V617M140 610V617M210 610V617M280 610V617M350 610V617M420 610V617'/></g><g text-anchor='middle'><text x='70' y='636'>0</text><text x='140' y='636'>10</text><text x='210' y='636'>20</text><text x='280' y='636'>30</text><text x='350' y='636'>40</text><text x='420' y='636'>50</text></g><g text-anchor='end'><text x='58' y='576'>5</text><text x='58' y='536'>10</text><text x='58' y='496'>15</text><text x='58' y='456'>20</text><text x='58' y='416'>25</text></g><text x='245' y='662' text-anchor='middle'>Waiting time (min)</text><text x='24' y='510' text-anchor='middle' transform='rotate(-90 24 510)'>Frequency</text></g></svg>", "number": "2", "question": ["The histograms show the waiting times (in minutes) of customers at Restaurant A and Restaurant B. Let $p$ be the percentage of customers who waited $x$ minutes or more.", "(1) For each restaurant, find $p$ when $x = 40$.", "(2) Use the class boundaries only. For each restaurant, find the value of $x$ for which $p$ is closest to $50\\%$.", "(3) Assume that the waiting times are uniformly distributed within each class. For each restaurant, estimate the value of $x$ for which $p = 50\\%$."], "section": "", "solution": ["(1) Restaurant A frequencies: $10$–$20$: $5$, $20$–$30$: $11$, $30$–$40$: $13$, $40$–$50$: $21$; total $= 50$.", "Restaurant B frequencies: $10$–$20$: $20$, $20$–$30$: $18$, $30$–$40$: $8$, $40$–$50$: $4$; total $= 50$.", "A: customers waiting $40$ min or more $= 21$, so $p = \\frac{21}{50} \\times 100\\% = 42\\%$.", "B: customers waiting $40$ min or more $= 4$, so $p = \\frac{4}{50} \\times 100\\% = 8\\%$.", "(2) A: at $x = 10, 20, 30, 40, 50$, $p = 100\\%, 90\\%, 68\\%, 42\\%, 0\\%$.", "Closest to $50\\%$ is $42\\%$ (difference $8$), so $x = 40$.", "B: at $x = 10, 20, 30, 40, 50$, $p = 100\\%, 60\\%, 24\\%, 8\\%, 0\\%$.", "Closest to $50\\%$ is $60\\%$ (difference $10$), so $x = 20$.", "(3) $p = 50\\%$ means $25$ of the $50$ customers waited $x$ min or more.", "A: $21$ waited $40$ or more, so $4$ more are needed from the $30$–$40$ class of $13$.", "$x = 40 - 10 \\times \\frac{4}{13} = \\frac{480}{13} \\approx 36.9$.", "B: $30$ waited $20$ or more, so $5$ must be removed from the $20$–$30$ class of $18$.", "$x = 20 + 10 \\times \\frac{5}{18} = \\frac{205}{9} \\approx 22.8$."], "topic": "Data and Uncertainty / Probability and Statistics", "type": "Worked example", "updatedAt": 1794904117506, "volume": "", "id": "ccjkxoa0l4l1f9pb2akb"}, {"answer": ["$-\\frac{4}{5}$"], "answer_figures": [], "book": "NDM", "category": "Procedure", "chapter": 2, "createdAt": 1794898821426, "figs_checked": false, "figure_svg": "", "number": "16", "question": ["$\\left(-\\frac{2}{3}\\right)\\div\\left[\\frac{1}{2}-\\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)\\right]$."], "section": "2.5", "solution": ["Evaluate the brackets first: $\\frac{1}{2}-\\left(-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{3}{6}+\\frac{2}{6}=\\frac{5}{6}$", "The expression becomes $\\left(-\\frac{2}{3}\\right)\\div\\frac{5}{6}$", "Dividing a negative number by a positive number gives a negative result. Multiply by the reciprocal: $-\\frac{2}{3}\\times\\frac{6}{5}$", "$=-\\frac{12}{15}=-\\frac{4}{5}$"], "topic": "", "type": "Worked example", "updatedAt": 1794905752105, "volume": "1", "id": "fk9sg9cbs2jo2v6plvmc"}, {"answer": ["The mean age is $14.8$ years."], "answer_figures": [], "book": "NDM", "category": "Procedure", "chapter": 12, "createdAt": 1794907213084, "figure_svg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 440 110\" width=\"440\" height=\"110\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"440\" height=\"110\" fill=\"white\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"15\" width=\"200\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#e6e6e6\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"15\" width=\"420\" height=\"80\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"10\" y1=\"55\" x2=\"430\" y2=\"55\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"210\" y1=\"15\" x2=\"210\" y2=\"95\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"265\" y1=\"15\" x2=\"265\" y2=\"95\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"320\" y1=\"15\" x2=\"320\" y2=\"95\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"375\" y1=\"15\" x2=\"375\" y2=\"95\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"42\" font-family=\"Times New Roman, serif\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"bold\">Age (<tspan font-style=\"italic\">x</tspan> years)</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"82\" font-family=\"Times New Roman, serif\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"bold\">Number of students</text><text x=\"237.5\" y=\"42\" font-family=\"Times New Roman, serif\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\">13</text><text x=\"292.5\" y=\"42\" font-family=\"Times New Roman, serif\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\">14</text><text x=\"347.5\" y=\"42\" font-family=\"Times New Roman, serif\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\">15</text><text x=\"402.5\" y=\"42\" font-family=\"Times New Roman, serif\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\">16</text><text x=\"237.5\" y=\"82\" font-family=\"Times New Roman, serif\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\">5</text><text x=\"292.5\" y=\"82\" font-family=\"Times New Roman, serif\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\">8</text><text x=\"347.5\" y=\"82\" font-family=\"Times New Roman, serif\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\">17</text><text x=\"402.5\" y=\"82\" font-family=\"Times New Roman, serif\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\">10</text></svg>", "number": "5", "question": ["The ages of a group of students are shown in the frequency table.", "Find the mean age of these students."], "section": "12.1", "solution": ["Total number of students: $5 + 8 + 17 + 10 = 40$", "Sum of ages: $13 \\times 5 + 14 \\times 8 + 15 \\times 17 + 16 \\times 10$", "$= 65 + 112 + 255 + 160 = 592$", "Mean $= \\frac{\\sum fx}{\\sum f} = \\frac{592}{40} = 14.8$", "The mean age is $14.8$ years."], "topic": "", "type": "Worked example", "variants": [{"answer": ["The mean age is $13.5$ years."], "answer_figures": [], "figure_svg": "<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 440 110\" width=\"440\" height=\"110\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"440\" height=\"110\" fill=\"white\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"15\" width=\"200\" height=\"80\" fill=\"#e6e6e6\"/><rect x=\"10\" y=\"15\" width=\"420\" height=\"80\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"10\" y1=\"55\" x2=\"430\" y2=\"55\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"210\" y1=\"15\" x2=\"210\" y2=\"95\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"265\" y1=\"15\" x2=\"265\" y2=\"95\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"320\" y1=\"15\" x2=\"320\" y2=\"95\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><line x1=\"375\" y1=\"15\" x2=\"375\" y2=\"95\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"20\" y=\"42\" font-family=\"Times New Roman, serif\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"bold\">Age (<tspan font-style=\"italic\">x</tspan> years)</text><text x=\"20\" y=\"82\" font-family=\"Times New Roman, serif\" font-size=\"20\" font-weight=\"bold\">Number of students</text><text x=\"237.5\" y=\"42\" font-family=\"Times New Roman, serif\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\">12</text><text x=\"292.5\" y=\"42\" font-family=\"Times New Roman, serif\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\">13</text><text x=\"347.5\" y=\"42\" font-family=\"Times New Roman, serif\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\">14</text><text x=\"402.5\" y=\"42\" font-family=\"Times New Roman, serif\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\">15</text><text x=\"237.5\" y=\"82\" font-family=\"Times New Roman, serif\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\">6</text><text x=\"292.5\" y=\"82\" font-family=\"Times New Roman, serif\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\">9</text><text x=\"347.5\" y=\"82\" font-family=\"Times New Roman, serif\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\">12</text><text x=\"402.5\" y=\"82\" font-family=\"Times New Roman, serif\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\">13</text></svg>", "question": ["The ages of a group of students are shown in the frequency table.", "Find the mean age of these students."], "solution": ["Total number of students: $6 + 9 + 12 + 13 = 40$", "Sum of ages: $12 \\times 6 + 13 \\times 9 + 14 \\times 12 + 15 \\times 13$", "$= 72 + 117 + 168 + 195 = 552$", "Mean $= \\frac{\\sum fx}{\\sum f} = \\frac{552}{40} = 13.8$", "The mean age is $13.8$ years."]}], "volume": "2", "id": "gkq6l3qdu9bt6is5lucy"}, {"answer": ["(a) $-1\\frac{4}{5}$", "(b) $1\\frac{11}{24}$"], "answer_figures": [], "book": "NDM", "category": "Procedure", "chapter": 2, "createdAt": 1794898524647, "figs_checked": false, "figure_svg": "", "number": "15", "question": ["(a) $-2\\frac{2}{5} \\times \\frac{3}{4}$", "(b) $1\\frac{7}{8} \\div \\left(1\\frac{2}{7}\\right)$"], "section": "2.5", "solution": ["(a) Convert the mixed number to an improper fraction: $-2\\frac{2}{5}=-\\frac{12}{5}$", "(a) Multiply: $-\\frac{12}{5}\\times\\frac{3}{4}=-\\frac{36}{20}$", "(a) Simplify: $-\\frac{36}{20}=-\\frac{9}{5}=-1\\frac{4}{5}$", "(b) Convert the mixed numbers to improper fractions: $1\\frac{7}{8}=\\frac{15}{8}$ and $1\\frac{2}{7}=\\frac{9}{7}$", "(b) Dividing by a fraction is the same as multiplying by its reciprocal: $\\frac{15}{8}\\div\\frac{9}{7}=\\frac{15}{8}\\times\\frac{7}{9}$", "(b) Cancel the common factor 3 and multiply: $\\frac{5}{8}\\times\\frac{7}{3}=\\frac{35}{24}$", "(b) Answer: $\\frac{35}{24}=1\\frac{11}{24}$"], "topic": "", "type": "Worked example", "updatedAt": 1794905492809, "volume": "1", "id": "oa0j9rcs6pedpja0ixpo"}, {"answer": ["(a) $19.588$", "(b) $38.885$", "(c) $19.53$"], "answer_figures": [], "book": "NDM", "category": "Procedure", "chapter": 2, "createdAt": 1794899792965, "figs_checked": false, "figure_svg": "", "number": "18", "question": ["(a) $13.65+5.938$", "(b) $47.3+(-8.415)$", "(c) $15.2-(-4.33)$"], "section": "2.5", "solution": ["(a) Line up the decimal points and write $13.65$ as $13.650$.", "$13.650+5.938=19.588$", "(b) Adding a negative number is the same as subtracting its positive.", "$47.3+(-8.415)=47.3-8.415$", "Write $47.3$ as $47.300$: $47.300-8.415=38.885$", "(c) Subtracting a negative number is the same as adding its positive.", "$15.2-(-4.33)=15.2+4.33$", "Write $15.2$ as $15.20$: $15.20+4.33=19.53$"], "topic": "", "type": "Worked example", "updatedAt": 1794906397893, "variants": [{"answer": ["(a) $25.776$", "(b) $7.492$", "(c) $7.92$", "(d) $10.35$"], "figure_svg": "", "question": ["(a) $18.426+7.35$", "(b) $14.072-6.58$", "(c) $7.05-(-0.87)$", "(d) $15+(-4.65)$"], "solution": ["(a) Line up the decimal points and write $7.35$ as $7.350$.", "$18.426+7.350=25.776$", "(b) Line up the decimal points and write $6.58$ as $6.580$.", "$14.072-6.580=7.492$", "(c) Subtracting a negative number is the same as adding its positive.", "$7.05-(-0.87)=7.05+0.87$", "$7.05+0.87=7.92$", "(d) Adding a negative number is the same as subtracting its positive.", "$15+(-4.65)=15-4.65$", "Write $15$ as $15.00$: $15.00-4.65=10.35$"]}], "volume": "1", "id": "ro54wwuevyo33md4fkxx"}, {"answer": ["(a) $-10.9$", "(b) $240.7$"], "answer_figures": [], "book": "NDM", "category": "Procedure", "chapter": 2, "createdAt": 1794900259012, "figs_checked": false, "figure_svg": "", "number": "20", "question": ["(a) $(-3.27)\\div 0.3$", "(b) $(-0.9628)\\div(-0.004)$"], "section": "2.5", "solution": ["(a) A negative divided by a positive gives a negative result.", "$3.27\\div 0.3 = \\frac{3.27}{0.3} = \\frac{32.7}{3} = 10.9$", "So $(-3.27)\\div 0.3 = -10.9$", "Check: $0.3\\times 10.9 = 3.27$", "(b) A negative divided by a negative gives a positive result.", "$0.9628\\div 0.004 = \\frac{0.9628}{0.004} = \\frac{962.8}{4} = 240.7$", "So $(-0.9628)\\div(-0.004) = 240.7$", "Check: $0.004\\times 240.7 = 0.9628$"], "topic": "", "type": "Worked example", "updatedAt": 1794906559492, "volume": "1", "id": "rp2p0sn6gtn0ua3hfv7w"}, {"answer": ["(a) $15.04$", "(b) $-0.02696$"], "answer_figures": [], "book": "NDM", "category": "Procedure", "chapter": 2, "createdAt": 1794900134472, "figs_checked": false, "figure_svg": "", "number": "19", "question": ["(a) $3.2 \\times 4.7$", "(b) $1.348 \\times (-0.02)$"], "section": "2.5", "solution": ["(a) Ignore the decimal points first: $32 \\times 47 = 1504$", "Count the decimal places: $3.2$ has $1$ and $4.7$ has $1$, so $1 + 1 = 2$ in total", "Put $2$ decimal places in the answer: $3.2 \\times 4.7 = 15.04$", "Check by estimating: $3 \\times 5 = 15$, so $15.04$ is reasonable", "(b) A positive number times a negative number gives a negative answer", "Ignore the decimal points first: $1348 \\times 2 = 2696$", "Count the decimal places: $1.348$ has $3$ and $0.02$ has $2$, so $3 + 2 = 5$ in total", "Put $5$ decimal places in the answer: $1.348 \\times 0.02 = 0.02696$", "So $1.348 \\times (-0.02) = -0.02696$", "Check by estimating: $1.35 \\times 0.02 = 0.027$, so $-0.02696$ is reasonable"], "topic": "", "type": "Worked example", "updatedAt": 1794906471692, "volume": "1", "id": "umh0ukhp48jbxd0xojk6"}, {"answer": ["(a) $\\frac{11}{20}$", "(b) $\\frac{3}{35}$"], "answer_figures": [], "book": "NDM", "category": "Problem solving", "chapter": 2, "createdAt": 1794905841933, "figure_svg": "", "number": "17", "question": ["In a conference, $\\frac{1}{4}$ of the participants are under the age of 15 and $\\frac{1}{5}$ of them are above 20 years old. Of those above 20 years old, $\\frac{4}{7}$ of them are women.", "Find the fraction of the participants who are", "(a) between 15 and 20 years old,", "(b) men above 20 years old."], "section": "2.5", "solution": ["(a) Fraction between 15 and 20 years old $= 1 - \\frac{1}{4} - \\frac{1}{5}$", "$= \\frac{20}{20} - \\frac{5}{20} - \\frac{4}{20}$", "$= \\frac{11}{20}$", "(b) Fraction of those above 20 who are men $= 1 - \\frac{4}{7} = \\frac{3}{7}$", "Fraction of participants who are men above 20 $= \\frac{3}{7} \\times \\frac{1}{5}$", "$= \\frac{3}{35}$"], "topic": "", "type": "Worked example", "volume": "1", "id": "x7k15cyd2l59zpoenxsa"}, {"answer": ["$y = 35$"], "answer_figures": [], "book": "NDM", "category": "Procedure", "chapter": 12, "createdAt": 1794906960936, "figure_svg": "", "number": "3", "question": ["The mean of $7$ numbers is $23$. Four of the numbers are $5$, $9$, $17$ and $25$. The other three numbers are each equal to $y$. Find the value of $y$."], "section": "12.1", "solution": ["Sum of all $7$ numbers $= 7 \\times 23 = 161$", "Sum of the four known numbers $= 5 + 9 + 17 + 25 = 56$", "The other three numbers add up to $3y$", "$56 + 3y = 161$", "$3y = 161 - 56 = 105$", "$y = \\frac{105}{3} = 35$", "Check: $\\frac{56 + 3 \\times 35}{7} = \\frac{161}{7} = 23$"], "topic": "", "type": "Worked example", "volume": "2", "id": "zwl3jyjwx4nkn4l5tsva"}]}